  "interpretation": [
    "The Fortress example uses the identical public own f4->f5 first move. Templates2/3/5/7 voluntarily move a7->a6; templates4/6 move f7->f6. No rank is disclosed in those quiet replies, and all8 templates satisfy either moved-origin mobility constraint. Action choice therefore carries formation information beyond that constraint.",
    "At decisions2 and3 the heldout classifier improves Flag log score under every one of the4 controlled own-policy contexts. This is a predictive mechanism observation, not a game-strength result.",
    "Do not add the per-step gains: each scores the entire correlated public prefix against the hard posterior at that step. Rank disclosures later make some Flags logically identified and reduce the available behavioral gain.",
    "The measured class frequency posterior is regularized and intentionally not claimed to be a calibrated exact Bayesian action likelihood for the DOS engine."
  ],
